# Discourse openings separated from the request by punctuation.
@reader.open.discourse pro.reader.body_lead role=neutral text="hey" text="one more thing" text="by the way"
# Immediately before an imperative, 'just' can soften a request. It can also
# restrict a scope, so the reader retains the original proposals.
@reader.open.imperative pro.reader.body_lead role=action_only text="just"
# Positive wishes or suggestions introducing a noun phrase. Property queries,
# exhibition, selection and standing preferences have different speech acts.
@reader.open.nominal pro.reader.body_lead role=nominal text="I want" text="I would like" text="I'd like" text="I would love" text="I'd love" text="how about"
